Cell["\<\
Caption: 0.1.0 extracts 28,833 unsound atoms (red); both fixes extract none, \
and the De Morgan split adds 27,351 sound atoms over the fix alone.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9e84d7a6-a606-492e-b0d0-e61f7b7286fb"],

Cell["Contradictions & Surprises", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"53049249-ddeb-421f-bc56-bb010343f190"],

Cell["\<\
The precision gap is sharper than the draft said: it occurs only where a leaf \
repeats, never otherwise (R4).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"534f4370-f159-4af2-a31c-cf784b1156cb"],

Cell["\<\
A bundled example carries the second root cause: rikyu_hpc a_submit_job \
blames launcher != 'mpirun' when launcher is None (R6).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4b9d66a3-fbbe-444d-859a-c9404823ce54"],

Cell["Steering Questions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9800fc2b-6baf-47f1-9c3b-655f2856308a"],

Cell["\<\
[now] Keep commit 3948b54 (De Morgan split)? It changes only sound atoms, \
making 17 bundled and 1,072 corpus actions finer.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b3c7c847-486b-4536-bcae-9727e75c4321"],

Cell["\<\
[now] File the control-flow source as its own issue, with R6 as its evidence.\
\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7acbb91f-7acd-4ff3-bbea-f2075a8a984e"],

Cell["\<\
[next run] Path-aware extraction: drop, or conjoin with their path condition, \
the atoms of ifs not reached on every successful path.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0e284f19-e42f-4f74-b4d0-104b6b668334"],

Cell["\<\
[later] Refresh the README coverage claim: 285/293 predates collections added \
since; the current count is 330/335.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fcbded90-e916-4ab8-82c0-47d000079061"],

Cell["Pointers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"dab35507-ad7b-45a3-8dd4-8981e6810815"],

Cell["\<\
Commits 185a327 (fix), 3948b54 (De Morgan split), 1e63e38 (release \
gtpyhop-diagnostics 0.1.1)\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"28ad24f6-d91d-42b3-afec-0c9c1527605a"],

Cell["tools/diagnostics_guard_check.py (8 cases, in checks.yml)", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"210f2b25-8fab-4c28-a1c4-1d29750b4c40"],

Cell["\<\
scripts/ next to this notebook: prop.py, examples_diff.py, corpus.py, cf.py \
